WEBVTT

00:00.700 --> 00:09.593
Cortex is memory for work: state, time and grounding, held in a live engine, so that a new session does not start the project over.

00:11.100 --> 00:14.407
A project is told to it in plain lines.

00:15.100 --> 00:16.666
Its scope.

00:16.716 --> 00:18.554
A checkpoint.

00:18.604 --> 00:21.315
What is expected of that checkpoint.

00:21.365 --> 00:23.815
And where it stands today.

00:23.865 --> 00:27.224
Each line is a run, with its own time.

00:31.100 --> 00:37.545
Each session reports what it did, as a line, and the engine reads it against what it already holds.

00:40.100 --> 00:44.036
Say a thing twice, and it is not stored twice.

00:44.086 --> 00:47.445
It is the same memory, with a new time.

00:48.500 --> 00:53.074
The next session starts from the state of the work, not from a transcript.

00:53.124 --> 00:54.793
Cortex.

00:54.843 --> 00:58.373
Research and engineering by James Huson.

00:58.423 --> 01:00.585
exnulla dot com.
